SCOPE LOCK RULES (MANDATORY — WHAT NOT TO TOUCH):
  ✗ NO globals.css changes
  ✗ NO homepage changes
  ✗ NO catalogue/VFS changes
  ✗ NO product page changes
  ✗ NO basket UI changes (BasketSummary.tsx styling stays)
  ✗ NO Sanity Studio configuration changes
  ✗ NO order management post-creation (out of scope)
  ✗ NO shipping cost calculation (hardcoded $15.99 stays for now)
  ✗ NO country list expansion (PL/GB stays for now)
  ✗ NO build runs except after final SC8 completion

EXECUTION MODEL — BACKEND SPRINT ADAPTATION:
  Pass 1 = Infrastructure (schema, types, clients)
  Pass 2 = Core Logic (business logic implementation)
  Pass 3 = Hardening (security, validation, error handling, tests)

  Sequencing: SC1 → SC2 → SC3 → SC4 → SC5 → SC6 → SC7 → SC8
  Each SC is BLOCKING — must pass verification before next SC begins.

LESSONS APPLIED AS ACTIVE CONSTRAINTS:
  ✓ Bus-stop methodology: Each SC maps to specific audit bus stops
  ✓ Schema verification: Run typegen before any GROQ/type work
  ✓ Functional grouping: Complete webhook handler (all events), not isolated
  ✓ Type consolidation: Single address mapper, single source of truth
  ✓ Verification gates: Dev server verification per SC, no builds until end
  ✓ No data assumptions: Verify actual Sanity data before GROQ changes
  ✓ GROQ syntax: brand->name NOT brand->{name} for reference derefs
  ✓ ES modules only: No require() in this codebase

