SCOPE CONTRACT 2: Checkout Route — Stock Reservation + Stripe Session
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Gap Coverage: C1 (Stripe disabled), C3 (phantom decrement), H1 (no reservation)
Bus Stops: 4, 5
Pass: 2 (Core Logic)
Depends On: SC1

TARGET STATE:
  POST /api/checkout:
    1. Validates publicBasket (array, non-empty, valid items)
    2. Fetches products via checkoutClient (non-CDN, fresh stock)
    3. Calculates availableStock = stock - reservedStock per item
    4. Checks availableStock >= requested quantity
    5. Atomically increments reservedStock via ifRevisionId (NOT dec stock)
    6. Creates Stripe checkout session with:
       - line_items from validated products
       - return_url: /checkout/return?session_id={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}
       - metadata.productsIntent: "productId:quantity,productId:quantity"
       - metadata.clerkUserId: user?.id || "guest"
       - expires_at: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 25 * 60
       - customer_email if authenticated
       - ui_mode: "embedded"
    7. Returns { client_secret: session.client_secret }
    8. On Stripe failure: ROLLBACK reservedStock (dec what was inc'd)
    9. On any error: ROLLBACK reservedStock + return appropriate status code

DoD (Sequenced):
  ☐ 2.1 Replace backendClient import with checkoutClient in route.ts
  ☐ 2.2 Uncomment and update Clerk currentUser() for metadata
  ☐ 2.3 Modify GROQ query: add reservedStock to product fetch projection
  ☐ 2.4 Replace stock decrement logic with reservedStock increment:
        — Calculate: availableStock = serverProduct.stock - (serverProduct.reservedStock || 0)
        — Check: availableStock >= clientItem.quantity
        — Patch: p.inc({ reservedStock: clientItem.quantity }).ifRevisionId(serverProduct._rev)
  ☐ 2.5 Uncomment and update Stripe session creation with all required params
  ☐ 2.6 Add rollback in catch block: for each reserved item, dec reservedStock
  ☐ 2.7 Add rollback between reservation commit and Stripe call (wrap Stripe in try/catch)
  ☐ 2.8 Return { client_secret: session.client_secret } on success
  ☐ 2.9 Verify: dev server, navigate to /checkout/payment — Stripe form loads

FILES TO MODIFY:
  app/api/checkout/route.ts (REWRITE — keep structure, replace logic)

CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:
  — NEVER dec({ stock }) in this route — only inc({ reservedStock })
  — Stock decrement happens ONLY in webhook on payment success
  — Rollback MUST happen if Stripe session creation fails
  — Use checkoutClient (non-CDN) for ALL queries in this route
  — ifRevisionId is MANDATORY for atomic reservation

VERIFICATION:
  Dev server running → navigate to /checkout/payment with basket items
  Stripe embedded form should appear (test mode)
  Check Sanity: product reservedStock incremented after checkout initiation
  Check: closing Stripe form does NOT decrement stock (only reservedStock was touched)

DELEGATION:
  /implement "SC2: Rewrite checkout route with stock reservation + Stripe session creation + rollback"

